      "fieldValue": "Picture 1 is the exact opening frame and controls the clean five-person compact asymmetric formation, 35mm left-front viewpoint, wet junction, layered spacing, reflections, and cyan-amber-red lighting. Picture 2 is Xiaoxin's identity and wardrobe reference: only the sharp large portrait controls the lead's face; the blurred standing views control his body, black survival clothing, harness, gloves, boots, and left-forearm bandage. Picture 3 preserves the same four distinct rescued men and their individual outfits; use it only to lock cast identity, not to replace Picture 1's opening formation. Reference Audio 1 is the exact chorus segment and controls the 136 BPM beat timing, Xiaoxin's Chinese singing mouth timing when his mouth is visible, and all cut accents.\n\nCreate a six-second cinematic, hard-hitting K-pop boy-group performance with exactly five young East Asian men and three clearly edited camera angles. Xiaoxin remains center lead and only singer, identified as (S1), singing <d>[Chinese] 我没有把你们忙丢，Hold on，马上就走。</d> The group has real momentum: no waiting in the opening pose, no long held formation before the first move, and every shot contains a readable four-to-eight-count choreography phrase. Use controlled travel and clean landing positions, not shaky camera tricks or acrobatics.\n\n[Shot 1] From 00:00.000 to 00:01.500, begin exactly from Picture 1 in a 32mm full-body medium-wide shot about 25 degrees left-front. The camera makes one smooth 25-degree dolly arc at a constant speed, with foreground shoulders creating parallax. Within the first quarter-second, all five hit a compact three-count phrase: Xiaoxin steps diagonally forward-right, pulls his bandaged left forearm down across his chest, then drives his right elbow out toward the central route; the four dancers answer in staggered cannon timing with separate half-steps, an inward arm pull, and a sharp shoulder hit. On the fourth count the whole group rebounds one clear half-step b